AB  - This is the presentation of the long paper "Silenced in the Data: Epistemic Injustice as Challenge for the AI-Assisted Analysis of Abuse in the Catholic Church" as presented at DH 2026 in Daejeon, South Korea on July 31st 2026. Abstract: This study examines epistemic injustice in Catholic Church abuse discourse, focusing on marginalized adult women survivors. Using AI-assisted methods, we create an annotated corpus, apply zero-shot relevance detection with generative LLMs, and perform fine-grained classification. Results reveal hidden patterns, data sparsity, and methodological strategies for analyzing small, imbalanced datasets. The project “Von Epistemic Injustice zu Epistemic Awareness. Prozessbasierte Methodenforschung zuMissbrauch an erwachsenen Frauen in der katholischen Kirche” (From Epistemic Injustice to EpistemicAwareness. Process‑based Methodological Research on Abuse of Adult Women in the Catholic Church) isfunded by the DFG (German Research Association, project number 539293243):https://missbrauchsmuster.de/forschen/projekte/forschungsprojekt-von-epistemic-injustice-zu-epistemic-awareness-prozessbasierte-methodenforschung-zu-missbrauch-an-erwachsenen-frauen-in-der-katholischen-kirche/ More information on the Missbrauchsmuster website.
